  "grade": "Original experimental release of hardware trajectory files and associated acquisition/plot code. FAIRINO exports are already processed and padded. No independent friction load-cell ground truth or matched pre/post rate-limited actuator command trace was established in these files.",
  "coverage": "Entire three trace directories in fixed revision: 12 FAIRINO files (138,051 rows), 11 Franka (407,191), and two Franka joint-compensation runs (33,912). The cartesian line slow file is absent from the Franka Robot Dataset directory; a processed figure comparison in another directory is not counted as a new original trajectory.",
  "native_fields": "Franka acquisition S-motion lines 109–125, 164–170, 225–255 export measured q and dq, desired acceleration ddq_d, and torque channel tau_J minus model gravity minus initial (measured tau_J minus initial gravity). This residual can contain dynamics, external interactions and modeling error. The controller uses libfranka limitRate with previous desired torque. The pre- and post-limiter commands are not exported as distinct file signals. FAIRINO collection program lines 59–99 reads six vendor joint angles/speeds/accelerations in degree-based units and vendor joint torques. Processed files in the release share seven-channel schema: joint-7 position/velocity/acceleration/torque zeros throughout. Conversion, filtering and a common across-platform calibration were not independently established; joint-channel statistics use source-native units.",
  "cleaning": "Read 21 identification files by header. Two Franka files (figure8_XZ_motion_kuaisu and xy_figure8_with_z_mansu) start immediately with 29 numeric fields. Apply sibling/collector field order and retain their first samples. Require all selected fields finite, report monotonic time. Omit padded FAIRINO axis 7 from torque/velocity distributions.",
